The choice of CPU (e.g., Intel vs. AMD) dictates the required motherboard socket (e.g., LGA 1700 vs. AM5). The motherboard chipset (e.g., Z790) then determines the supported RAM type (DDR4 or DDR5). A high-end GPU (e.g., RTX 4090) has a minimum power requirement, constraining the choice of Power Supply (PSU) to 850W or higher. The GPU's physical length (e.g., 350mm) must also be compatible with the case's maximum GPU clearance. Finally, the case (e.g., ATX, Micro-ATX) must match the motherboard's form factor, and an optional large air cooler's height must be less than the case's CPU cooler clearance.